# How to cite foehn. GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository".
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use foehn in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "foehn: a Python toolkit for MeteoSwiss Open Government Data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hendriksen
    given-names: Kay
repository-code: "https://github.com/kayhendriksen/foehn"
url: "https://kayhendriksen.github.io/foehn/"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-10-25"
keywords:
  - meteoswiss
  - weather
  - climate
  - open-data
  - switzerland
  - parquet
  - xarray
abstract: >-
  foehn downloads every MeteoSwiss Open Government Data collection through the
  STAC API, converts station CSVs to Parquet with Polars, opens gridded NetCDF,
  GRIB2 and ODIM radar data as xarray Datasets or Zarr stores, and serves the
  data to LLMs through a Model Context Protocol server.
